sequenceDiagram
  participant C as Client (user of Tenant A)
  participant V as DRF view (TenantScopedMixin / ProjectScopedMixin)
  participant P as WorkspaceMembershipPermission
  participant D as PostgreSQL
  C->>V: GET /api/workspaces/{ws}/projects/{p}/issues/
  V->>P: has_permission(request)
  P->>D: Membership WHERE user = session user AND workspace = {ws}
  alt no membership
    P-->>C: 404 (existence not revealed)
  else membership found
    P->>P: role allowed for this HTTP method? (else 403)
    P->>D: Project WHERE id = {p} AND workspace = membership.workspace
    alt project missing / no project access
      P-->>C: 404
    else ok
      V->>D: Issues WHERE workspace = membership.workspace AND project = {p}
      D-->>C: only Tenant A rows
    end
  end
  Note over C,D: Client-supplied tenant ids are never trusted: the workspace is re-derived from the session user's membership on every request. Body ids (status, sprint, assignee...) are validated against the same project.
